    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most consistent weaknesses in the UBI argument often revolve around its immense cost and potential inflationary impact. Opponents will argue that the funding required is unsustainable and that injecting large amounts of cash without productivity gains could devalue currency. A strong rebuttal is to pivot the discussion to the *cost of current poverty programs*, arguing that UBI simplifies and replaces inefficient, bureaucratic welfare redundancies. Furthermore, they should challenge the assumption that people will simply use free time for productive endeavors, suggesting motivation and the labor force participation rate are serious concerns.",
