      "content": "When they invoke \"human dignity,\" aggressively reframe it as an entitlement that undermines personal responsibility, not true dignity. Argue that genuine dignity is found in productive contribution and self-sufficiency, not in passive government handouts. You can counter the anxiety argument by pointing to the risk of dependency: a lack of necessity encourages stagnation, leading to a populace that is psychologically reliant on the state rather than empowered by opportunity. Essentially, paint UBI not as liberation, but as a gilded cage incentivizing societal decay.",
